preface: whole, followed by SETTINGS, in part, and an HTTP/1.1 request
round trips: DATA, HEADERS, PRIORITY, RST_STREAM, SETTINGS and its ACK, PUSH_PROMISE, PING, GOAWAY, WINDOW_UPDATE
padding and priorities: padded DATA, padded HEADERS with a priority, the reserved bit, an unknown type
a 40000-byte field block: HEADERS and 2 CONTINUATIONs, the last with END_HEADERS; PUSH_PROMISE's leaves room for the promised stream
incomplete: every prefix of a frame asks for more
errors:
  DATA longer than SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE: FRAME_SIZE_ERROR, connection
  DATA on stream 0: PROTOCOL_ERROR, connection
  DATA padded past its end: PROTOCOL_ERROR, connection
  DATA padded with no pad length: FRAME_SIZE_ERROR, connection
  HEADERS on stream 0: PROTOCOL_ERROR, connection
  HEADERS too short for its priority: FRAME_SIZE_ERROR, connection
  HEADERS depending on itself: PROTOCOL_ERROR, stream
  PRIORITY on stream 0: PROTOCOL_ERROR, connection
  PRIORITY of 4 bytes: FRAME_SIZE_ERROR, stream
  PRIORITY depending on itself: PROTOCOL_ERROR, stream
  RST_STREAM on stream 0: PROTOCOL_ERROR, connection
  RST_STREAM of 3 bytes: FRAME_SIZE_ERROR, connection
  SETTINGS on stream 1: PROTOCOL_ERROR, connection
  SETTINGS ACK with parameters: FRAME_SIZE_ERROR, connection
  SETTINGS of 5 bytes: FRAME_SIZE_ERROR, connection
  PUSH_PROMISE on stream 0: PROTOCOL_ERROR, connection
  PUSH_PROMISE too short for its stream: FRAME_SIZE_ERROR, connection
  PING on stream 1: PROTOCOL_ERROR, connection
  PING of 7 bytes: FRAME_SIZE_ERROR, connection
  GOAWAY on stream 1: PROTOCOL_ERROR, connection
  GOAWAY of 7 bytes: FRAME_SIZE_ERROR, connection
  WINDOW_UPDATE of 3 bytes: FRAME_SIZE_ERROR, connection
  WINDOW_UPDATE of 0 on the connection: PROTOCOL_ERROR, connection
  WINDOW_UPDATE of 0 on a stream: PROTOCOL_ERROR, stream
  CONTINUATION on stream 0: PROTOCOL_ERROR, connection
settings refused:
  setting 0002 = 00000002: PROTOCOL_ERROR
  setting 0004 = 80000000: FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR
  setting 0005 = 00003fff: PROTOCOL_ERROR
  setting 0005 = 01000000: PROTOCOL_ERROR
  setting 0008 = 00000002: PROTOCOL_ERROR
  setting 0009 = 00000002: PROTOCOL_ERROR
settings: unknown ones ignored, the last of a repeated one kept, the limits taken
